    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d220">

                <pb facs="0381" n="293" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg293"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/2965: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wheeler</hi>)<anchor n="76"
                        xml:id="d220-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-03-22T14:00:00-05:00">March 22, 1933—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9. Neutral Commission has been requested by the representatives of the neighbors
                    to join in immediate representations to Bolivia and Paraguay to bring about
                    cessation of hostilities. They state that Bolivia <pb facs="0382" n="294"
                        xml:id="pg294"/> and Paraguay have accepted in principle the Mendoza formula
                    and in view thereof they believe that further peace negotiations can be better
                    carried out if they could obtain the consent of Bolivia and Paraguay for the
                    immediate cessation of hostilities for 60 days. Peruvian Ambassador makes the
                    reservation that the armistice should be on the basis that both parties will
                    maintain their actual respective positions without their forces being obliged to
                    withdraw.</p>
                <p>Please cable as soon as possible views of Government to which you are accredited
                    regarding this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d220-f1" n="76" type="source" xml:id="d220-f1-content">
                <p>The same, March 22, 2 p.m., to the Minister in Bolivia as telegram No. 6.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
